      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a really solid, professional draft. It definitely hits the right tone for a real employee to use.\n\nThe thing is, I just ran that draft through the `positivity_index` tool we use for the manual, and it came back with a pretty mediocre score—it's only sitting at about 0.65. For the \"Gold Standard\" section of our training module, the directors are really looking for examples that hit the 0.9 or 0.95 range to show what \"peak positivity\" looks like under the new initiative.\n\nCould you try a second version? Don't make it unprofessional or weird, but try to push that positivity index much higher. We need it to be a clear standout for the high-scorers list.",
